WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:07.013
This JSON record is self-describing because the keys
tell us what each value represents But

00:00:07.026 --> 00:00:12.476
it is not a flat table Heart rate is nested inside
metrics and latitude and

00:00:12.503 --> 00:00:18.201
longitude are nested inside location A second record
could add oxygen

00:00:18.227 --> 00:00:23.744
saturation or omit sleep hours Before analysis we
often

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:29.650
flatten the JSON into columns But flattening is only
a structural step

00:00:30.574 --> 00:00:36.087
We still need to understand units missingness and
the analytical meaning of the extracted fields
